      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is more about the mechanical signaling and neurological adaptation than boredom. Consistent heavy loading can lead to neuromuscular accommodation, where the nervous system learns to perform the movement without significant adaptation. Changing rep ranges, exercise variations, or tempo forces different motor unit recruitment and increases specific mechanical tension in novel ways, prompting further hypertrophic or strength gains.",
      "source": "target",
