    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. so it's basically about keeping the body from getting too efficient at the specific movement so we can force more growth. i'll try to explain the neurological part to them. one more thing though—they've mentioned it feels like they're hitting a wall that's almost... i don't know, stubborn? like, they're doing everything right but the progress just isn't there. is there any chance this could be more than just physiological fatigue, like something else messing with their rhythm or energy?",
